  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_LeastPrivilege  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_LeastPrivilege.als
    rationale: Clearing F_LeastPrivilege removes the (role, op) ↔ outcome=Success linkage; the injection forces a successful operation whose (role, kind) cell is NOT in PermMatrix.Allowed — exactly what LeastPrivilege forbids.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyEvents  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_AppendOnlyEvents.als
    rationale: Clearing the append-only fact removes the uniqueness constraint on (app, event_type); the injection forces two distinct events with identical (app, event_type) — a direct counterexample to append-only.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_016_AuditAppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditAppendOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OnePendingPerCustomer  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_OnePendingPerCustomer.als
    rationale: Clearing F_OnePendingPerCustomer lets a customer hold two Pending-Review applications simultaneously; the injection demands exactly that scenario.
    expected to FAIL: FR_005_OnePendingPerCustomer
      - FR_005_OnePendingPerCustomer: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AtMostOneDecisionPerApp  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_AtMostOneDecisionPerApp.als
    rationale: Clearing the at-most-one-decision-per-app fact allows two Decision rows pointing at the same LoanApplication; the injection forces two such Decisions to exist, violating FR-011/FR-012.
    expected to FAIL: FR_011_AtMostOneDecision, FR_012_NoDualDecision
      - FR_011_AtMostOneDecision: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_NoDualDecision: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OwnershipBasedAccess  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_OwnershipBasedAccess.als
    rationale: Clearing F_OwnershipBasedAccess lets a customer's GetApplicationById succeed without a properly-owned target; the injection produces a customer Success on GetApplicationById with NO target, which the predicate insists must have an owned target — and F_NoInformationLeakage (which requires `some op.target`) does not constrain this case.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_013_CustomerScoping
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_013_CustomerScoping: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AttributionCorrect  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_AttributionCorrect.als
    rationale: Clearing F_AttributionCorrect removes the rule that a SubmittedEvent's actor must equal the application's customer; the injection forces a SubmittedEvent whose recorded actor differs from the application's customer.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)

